      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name blends California, Nevada, and Arizona, reflecting its tri‑state border location.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Cal-Nev-Ari,_Nevada",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Kidwell Airport’s 4,140‑foot sand runway began as a World War II emergency strip and now serves the community.",
